            "prompt": "Build a production-grade backend service that generates dynamic GitHub statistics cards as SVG images.\n\n## Objective\n\nCreate a FastAPI-based service that:\n\n* Fetches GitHub user data using GraphQL (primary) and REST (fallback)\n* Computes statistics such as:\n\n  * Total contributions (from contribution calendar)\n  * Current contribution streak\n  * Longest contribution streak\n* Renders the data into a styled SVG card (similar to GitHub Readme Stats UI)\n* Returns the SVG as an HTTP response\n* Supports caching and rate-limit protection for reliability\n\n---\n\n## Tech Stack\n\n* Backend: Python with FastAPI (async)\n* HTTP client: httpx (async)\n* Cache: Redis\n* Background jobs: optional (use simple async tasks or Celery if needed)\n* Deployment target: containerized (Docker-ready)\n\n---\n\n## API Requirements\n\n### Endpoint\n\nGET /stats?username={github_username}\n\n### Response\n\n* Content-Type: image/svg+xml\n* Returns a fully rendered SVG card\n\n---\n\n## GitHub Integration\n\n### Use:\n\n* GitHub GraphQL API (primary)\n* GitHub REST API (fallback)\n\n### Authentication:\n\n* Use a GitHub Personal Access Token from environment variable:\n  GITHUB_TOKEN\n\n### GraphQL Query Requirements:\n\nFetch:\n\n* contributionCalendar (total contributions + daily data)\n* repositories (optional: stars, languages if needed later)\n\n---\n\n## Data Processing\n\n### Contribution Streak Logic:\n\n* Input: daily contribution calendar (date + count)\n* Compute:\n\n  1. Current streak:\n\n     * Count consecutive days from today backwards where contributions > 0\n  2. Longest streak:\n\n     * Max consecutive days with contributions > 0\n* Ignore future dates\n* Handle timezone safely (use UTC)\n\n---\n\n## Caching (MANDATORY)\n\n### Redis usage:\n\n* Cache key: stats:{username}\n* TTL: 15 minutes\n\n### Strategy:\n\n1. On request:\n\n   * Check Redis\n   * If hit → return cached SVG\n2. If miss:\n\n   * Fetch from GitHub\n   * Compute stats\n   * Store in Redis\n   * Return SVG\n\n### Fallback:\n\n* If GitHub API fails:\n\n  * Return last cached data if available\n  * Otherwise return a minimal error SVG\n\n---\n\n## SVG Rendering\n\n### Requirements:\n\n* Pure SVG string (no external dependencies)\n* Fixed layout similar to:\n\n  * Left: Total Contributions\n  * Center: Current Streak (highlighted circle)\n  * Right: Longest Streak\n* Dark theme\n* Responsive via viewBox\n\n### No frontend required\n\n---\n\n## Performance Requirements\n\n* Response time target: <200ms (with cache)\n* Avoid recomputation on every request\n* Use async requests for GitHub calls\n\n---\n\n## Error Handling\n\n* Handle:\n\n  * GitHub API rate limits\n  * Invalid usernames\n  * Network failures\n* Always return valid SVG (never raw JSON errors)\n\n---\n\n## Project Structure\n\n* app/\n\n  * main.py (FastAPI entry)\n  * github.py (API calls)\n  * services/\n    stats.py (calculation logic)\n    cache.py (Redis logic)\n    svg.py (SVG generator)\n  * models/ (optional)\n* requirements.txt\n* Dockerfile\n\n---\n\n## Environment Variables\n\n* GITHUB_TOKEN\n* REDIS_URL\n\n---\n\n## Optional Enhancements (design for extensibility)\n\n* Add profile views counter (store in Redis)\n* Add language stats\n* Add stars / repo metrics\n* Add themes (dark/light)\n\n---\n\n## Constraints\n\n* Do NOT use blocking code\n* Do NOT recompute stats if cached\n* Do NOT call multiple REST endpoints when GraphQL can fetch in one request\n* Keep logic modular and testable\n\n---\n\n## Deliverables\n\n* Fully working FastAPI app\n* Redis integration\n* GraphQL integration\n* Accurate streak calculation\n* SVG output matching GitHub stats style\n* Ready to deploy with Docker\n\n---\n\nWrite clean, production-ready code with clear separation of concerns and no unnecessary abstractions.\n"
